# --- SECRETS — never commit these ---
.env
*key*
*keys*

# --- Mac clutter ---
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
._*
**/._*

# --- Temp / runtime files ---
*.tmp
*.bak
*.pyc
__pycache__/

# Safety-copies made before a risky edit (ohbot_chat.py.backup and friends).
# These are snapshots of THIS machine's work-in-progress. Sharing them would
# push half-finished code to the Pi and clutter every diff. Added 2026-08-12.
*.backup
*.orig
*.rej

# --- SAMBA leftovers + cleanup quarantine ---
.smbdelete*
**/.smbdelete*
_trash_cleanup/

# --- Python virtual environment ---
venv/
.venv/

# --- Personal / project-specific docs (not for public repo) ---
CLAUDE.md
HANDOFF_*.md
README_github.md
README_ohbot_assistant.md
Ohbot\ Pi\ 4.txt

# --- Per-machine files (NOT shared between the Mac and the Pi) ---
# These record what THIS machine last did, or are calibration scratch copies.
# Keeping them out of git is deliberate: if they were shared, pulling on the
# Pi would overwrite the Pi's own calibration with the Mac's, which has caused
# trouble before. Real robot profiles live in ohbotData/robots/ and ARE shared.
ohbotData/active_robot.txt
ohbotData/language.txt
# THE LIVE CALIBRATION FILE. Added 2026-08-13.
# This is the one yobot_core.py actually reads, so it decides how far every
# motor on THIS machine's robot is allowed to move. It was tracked by git
# until now, which was the very hazard the comment above warns about — the
# scratch copies were excluded but the real file was missed. With Windows
# holding one robot and the Mac holding another, a push from one machine
# followed by a pull on the other would have handed the second robot the
# first robot's mouth. Each machine keeps its own now.
# The shared robot library in ohbotData/robots/ is still tracked, and that
# is where a calibration you want on every machine belongs. To set this
# machine up, load a robot from that library rather than pulling this file.
ohbotData/MotorDefinitionsv21.omd
ohbotData/MD_old_*.omd
ohbotData/MD_Goldie.omd
ohbotData/MD_blueboy.omd
ohbotData/MD_before_3point_backup.omd
ohbotData/archive/
# If one of these ever turns out to be a robot you want to share, don't delete
# the line — copy the file into ohbotData/robots/ instead, which is tracked.

# --- Log files (runtime output, per-machine — see ohbot_logging.py) ---
# Each program writes logs/<name>-<date>.log. They're this machine's record of
# what happened, not shared code, and they'd be noisy in the repo.
logs/

# --- Large binary / archive files ---
*.zip
*.docx

# --- Original library-specific knowledge base ---
library_knowledge.json

# --- Library-specific bot files (generic versions are ohbot_chat.py / ohbotchat_server.py) ---
ohbot_conversation.py
ohbot_server.py

# --- Docs that are project-specific or planning notes ---
docs/Azure_Latency_Handoff.md
docs/Ohbot_shop_handofff.md
docs/FUTURE_events_system_outline.md
docs/SAMBA_COWORK_SETUP.md
PiOS_Headless_Optimization_Guide.md
docs/power_hardening.md

# --- The root index.html (it lives in gui/ for the repo) ---
/index.html

# --- Sequences folder (created at runtime by the GUI) ---
# Uncomment the next line if you don't want to share your saved sequences
# sequences/
_audio_check_*.wav

# Windows desktop shortcuts - local to one PC, no use to anyone else
*.lnk

# temporary holding folder - safe to trash
_to_delete/

# The *key* / *keys* rules above are a deliberately wide net for secrets.
# This one file is a GUIDE about getting keys, not a key. Let it through.
!Getting your API keys.md

